You must strictly enforce the following security, performance, and structural guidelines across all projects:

Data Security & Backend Integrity
Hide API keys and purge all Git secrets from code outputs.

Utilize public database keys safely and enforce strict Row-Level Security (RLS).

Encrypt sensitive user data and hash passwords securely.

Enforce server-side authentication, lock record access, and restrict database permissions.

Block field tampering and validate all incoming data inputs.

