Frontend Performance, Structure, & Compliance
Enforce strict Content Security Policy (CSP) headers and HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS).

Ensure absolute WCAG 2.1 AA compliance covering contrast ratios, semantic ARIA attributes, and complete keyboard navigation.

Optimize all vanilla JavaScript for maximum execution speed, eliminating unnecessary loops and redundant DOM queries.

Keep all inline or block CSS completely modular, scoped, and free of redundant style declarations using consistent design system tokens (CSS variables for spacing, typography, and color).

Implement graceful degradation and robust fallbacks for legacy or non-supporting browser environments.

Maintain strict code consistency by adhering to uniform indentation, naming conventions, and clean modular file organization.

Optimize bundle size and asset delivery by avoiding heavy third-party libraries when native browser APIs suffice, ensuring compressed asset handling.

Force HTTPS usage, scan dependencies regularly, and add standard security header configurations.


